# Release-gate evidence. Written by a gate run, so it appears in whatever
# directory the run was pointed at -- which for a local run is inside the
# working tree. These are artefacts of a QA run, never sources: the Android
# gate defaults its evidence dir to `.` and the Linux gate to
# ./linux-smoke-evidence, so without this a single local run leaves untracked
# files that look like a change. Ignored rather than deleted, because the
# evidence is the point of the gate and a reviewer's machine should not have to
# remember to preserve it.
/android-smoke-evidence/
/linux-smoke-evidence/

# The interpreter venv `make venv` builds for the hash-pinned test suites.
# Ignored so a developer's local venv cannot be committed by accident.
.venv-test/
.venv/
